# Cross-platform & remote Nests

Hatchery must run as a **host** on Linux, macOS, and Windows, and manage **Nests** (local or remote): libvirt/KVM, UTM, Hyper-V. Epic: [#202](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/202).

**Architecture (locked):** [Host plane vs Nest plane](../../.hatchery/docs/architecture-nests.md) — one product shell; Nest providers are first-class optional modules. Do not fork into three apps; do not bypass Nest registry/factory once they land (#207 / #206).

## Two planes

| Plane | Own |
|---|---|
| **Host** | App runtime, UI, Settings, DB, Library, orchestration, Nest transport client |
| **Nest** | Hypervisor lifecycle via `BaseProvider` (libvirt / UTM / Hyper-V × local or remote) |

Host requirements ≠ Nest-local tool requirements (#208). Libvirt-only rules stay in the libvirt adapter.

## Multi-OS CI (required)

PR acceptance runs the **portable** pytest suite on **ubuntu-latest**, **macos-latest**, and **windows-latest** (`.github/workflows/test.yml`). Coverage gate applies on each OS (`pyproject.toml`).

- Do **not** add host-OS-only assumptions that break CI on another runner
- Tests that need a real Nest/hypervisor use `@pytest.mark.hypervisor` and are **excluded** from CI (`-m "not hypervisor"`)
- Mock Nest transport and provider subprocesses in the default suite

```
✅ Pathlib, mocked virsh/ssh, skipif for optional tools (e.g. pwsh)
❌ Hard-code /usr/bin/… or apt-only checks in portable code paths under test
❌ New “integration” tests that require KVM/UTM/Hyper-V without the hypervisor mark
```

## Always ask

```
✅ Does this work on Linux, macOS, and Windows Hatchery hosts?
✅ Does this assume a local Nest only, or also remote?
✅ Are OS-specific paths (apt, xdg-open, systemd, .desktop) behind a portable helper?
✅ Did you update `.hatchery/docs/providers.md` if Nest/provider capability changed?
✅ Does this go through Nest id → factory once #206/#207 exist (not hard-wired libvirt)?
```

```
❌ Bake apt/dpkg, xdg-open, or systemd as the only path
❌ Hard-wire LibvirtProvider when the call should go through the Nest factory (#206)
❌ Treat Mac/Windows as afterthoughts or permanent sys.platform product shims
❌ Three divergent products instead of modular Nest adapters
```
